#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119616 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119805 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "fd3cb5b1-f16e-5a52-82e4-25bbbd1c4fe7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4789" :question/problem "Find $s,$ if $3\\mathbf{a_1}+s\\mathbf{a_2} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n![](images/df/df62636427555a986454d8d2787e110eb664771f5a74a38fdaa99ec593643729.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $s$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+s{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $s=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119617 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119806 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "548ef945-392b-5e75-9b60-14f4e2de6261" :question/math-academy-id "e-4790" :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf{x},$ if $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n![](images/93/93311059b2929dfac5a7dc2019e4591534fdcf3c416486ffdfc78ece16901ca4.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $\\mathbf{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+2x & =b \\\\ 2x & =b-a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(b-a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119618 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119807 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "13ebde04-8518-5837-9420-c9487debc562" :question/math-academy-id "e-4791" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n![](images/cc/cc8a77d53637f5523dcdadd79ea3a282efe30b96aaeb9ec31fce1f39d4006186.png)\n\nIf $x_1 \\mathbf{c}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{c}_2  = \\mathbf d,$ then what is $x_1+x_2?$" :question/worked-solution "If $x_1 \\mathbf{c}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{c}_2  = \\mathbf d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -{x}_{1}=-5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain $x_1=5,$ which we substitute into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ 4(5)+{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x_1=5$ and $x_2=-15$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 3(5)+(-15) & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is $x_1=5$ and $x_2=-15,$ which means\n\n$$\n5 \\mathbf{c_1}-15 \\mathbf{c_2} = \\mathbf{d}.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2=5-15=-10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119669 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119854 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "d9beff9d-db58-540f-811e-a07fb77d3d92" :question/math-academy-id "e-6191" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n![](images/9f/9f5f9de266fac1e593ea58a3406ff88ccecb3a64963d55367297404360771d83.png)\n\nIf $x_1 \\mathbf{a}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{a}_2 + x_3\\mathbf{a}_3 = \\mathbf b,$ then what is $x_1+x_2+x_3?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\mathbf{b}$ is a linear combination of vectors $\\mathbf{a_1}, \\,\\mathbf{a_2}$ and $\\mathbf{a_3}$ with coefficients $x_1,\\, x_2$ and $x_3,$ respectively, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n![](images/4d/4d3cb5eb82dd012582c78fc2c1201c62f99779d92974aba2a61f5a6bce8b91b9.png)\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 = 2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_2 = -1,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_3=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+2(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_1 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo the solution of the system is $x_1=-3, x_2=-1, x_3=2,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3 \\mathbf{a_1}- \\mathbf{a_2} +2 \\mathbf{a_3}= \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2+x_3=-3-1+2=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119806 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55242c77-3e41-5fa2-b4bb-748f8cda0851" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238791} {:answer/id #uuid "5c71a2b1-85ca-5099-8f54-6e98685b9f3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238863} {:answer/id #uuid "b3e09a56-8be6-5f0b-a232-4fefca913f23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239626} {:answer/id #uuid "ee094296-26d3-56b8-8c76-a17091ddddcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240152} {:answer/id #uuid "fd7a4f06-5e87-52ca-9c4b-04bdd6d58484" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c71a2b1-85ca-5099-8f54-6e98685b9f3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238863} :answer-field/id #uuid "a319c274-8067-5830-8026-4fd1f3678588" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0970eb33-9f16-5468-a48a-ce3c4e9ea202" :question/math-academy-id "q-105159" :question/problem "Find $x$, if $4a+3x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a+3x & =b \\\\ 3x & =b-4a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}(b-4a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119806 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "477c777c-4fcf-504a-b88b-0251c8d7a259" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238678} {:answer/id #uuid "6e63b088-eae4-5df4-a692-469894ca6ec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239006} {:answer/id #uuid "7f9b6079-8d41-5d56-a4ff-12d7e702dec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239167} {:answer/id #uuid "b78c0e7b-505a-54ad-9372-3b394b39ce62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239654} {:answer/id #uuid "e676cf21-c546-5aee-9ff8-268bb691b292" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f9b6079-8d41-5d56-a4ff-12d7e702dec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239167} :answer-field/id #uuid "31ef6744-d09a-5274-adfa-0de0cc8cac5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "665aac1d-ba76-55e8-8058-f38999b08deb" :question/math-academy-id "q-105161" :question/problem "Find the value of ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$ given that $7a+4x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7a+4x & =b \\\\ 4x & =b-7a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}(b-7a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}([\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]-7[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-2-1=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119807 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05c3a1ce-60e5-59ff-a50a-13acd330b03f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238128} {:answer/id #uuid "16ccfa6d-4cbd-58be-a3d1-40e500abddf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238250} {:answer/id #uuid "489d3697-4f9a-5294-985c-5ec2c27fe312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238688} {:answer/id #uuid "51497961-e6a7-5e4d-9d38-e1cc46624ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238757} {:answer/id #uuid "bb3b3d4a-ea4e-52ba-aaca-a3a81abdfca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb3b3d4a-ea4e-52ba-aaca-a3a81abdfca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239685} :answer-field/id #uuid "418087c6-543a-58e8-a946-98e11e2f5b50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d5149dd7-ead1-5d7c-a754-e514e2e6e606" :question/math-academy-id "q-105167" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-7{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the first and the second equations we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} & =-6 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we substitute into the second equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+5(3) & =3 \\\\ -3{x}_{1} & =-12 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2}=3$ into the third equation and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ (4)-(3) & =1 \\\\ 1 & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2}=3,$ which means\n\n$$\n4{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4+3=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119854 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "023fcb6e-19a9-5e78-8982-04f818ca611a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238099} {:answer/id #uuid "04fb8f1e-74de-53e7-811e-89afaef85a39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238122} {:answer/id #uuid "60fcd9a2-4983-563f-a7a0-4d01c2393643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238907} {:answer/id #uuid "b211c6b0-fbe0-52d2-9297-1454f53b6452" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239610} {:answer/id #uuid "f512eece-de08-5c13-ae53-369aa60ff55b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "023fcb6e-19a9-5e78-8982-04f818ca611a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238099} :answer-field/id #uuid "257c3c3e-fb71-526d-8119-cd61bd75c90e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2b7aaa73-fdec-536a-866a-953c6856f39f" :question/math-academy-id "q-105169" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 5{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 6{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{3} \\\\ -8{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3}=-3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & -8 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & -8 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -13 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=-13 \\\\ 0=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0=8$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119807 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6d66bec-4f70-53d2-9ff4-2520b4c8cdf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117898} {:answer/id #uuid "f4d4957d-eb5a-5c29-b427-cd7789e9a7a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117899} {:answer/id #uuid "2eb48522-7684-5c49-9b22-80599f5f6575" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117900} {:answer/id #uuid "55c5a60b-30f3-5dd0-8c86-12e610e70a02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117901} {:answer/id #uuid "5f15135e-67c9-596b-bf5d-2210d31c2fb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117902}] :answer-field/id #uuid "eb5fae5b-0364-5098-baba-4caac87e9d00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117897}] :question/id #uuid "b9323edd-e697-569c-8dd2-3fe5f9eed059" :question/math-academy-id "q-34054" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$a_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}, a_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nIf $x_{1}a_{1} + x_{2}a_{2} = b$, then what is $x_{1} + x_{2}$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319047 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119805 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ef7a933-e25a-53f9-8029-20032af40044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317617} {:answer/id #uuid "9b77d5ab-caa5-55ab-a2eb-19df2a01588b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318096} {:answer/id #uuid "a345a44b-c232-5f9b-95d9-d833914ac12c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318125} {:answer/id #uuid "a5f4c69f-a3d2-5b2e-a4f1-2cbf710d3530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318136} {:answer/id #uuid "db5fd3b6-f534-51c2-8e4a-d49452bf7c7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b77d5ab-caa5-55ab-a2eb-19df2a01588b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318096} :answer-field/id #uuid "18122832-a71e-5571-885b-b5abdf5b4fd3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3695980d-a1ca-52c3-a275-096dc38f4d3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-34602" :question/problem "Find $k$, if $8{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=0$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $k$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 8[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+k[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-8[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -48 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the first components, we get \n\n$$\n-2k=24\\,⟹\\,k=-12.\n$$\n\nBut then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 48\\end{aligned}]\\ne [\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -48 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there is no $k$ such that \n $8{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342134 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119854 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c3b744a-01a9-54ce-8529-5a08f78940d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339816} {:answer/id #uuid "60e09ff1-d3cc-58ef-8987-5a5f148e2536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339992} {:answer/id #uuid "8a3631e7-ceb5-57d9-884a-4e22407dcb9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340363} {:answer/id #uuid "9ad3c54b-5811-537d-84b5-61c05d4666df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340526} {:answer/id #uuid "a932259c-57be-54ad-a6fe-9cb2e6f3f068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a932259c-57be-54ad-a6fe-9cb2e6f3f068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340667} :answer-field/id #uuid "84898483-2191-5459-b5c9-62b59dd71df8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "118e9ea0-84b3-5e8f-866f-104da032b6d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-74035" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ 5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=4 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0.2 & 0.8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0.2 & 0.8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}+\\,0.2{x}_{3}=0.8 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+0.2(-1)=0.8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\n   \n\nFinally,  substituting ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(1)=-3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-2$, ${x}_{2}=1$, and ${x}_{3}=-1,$ which means  \n\n$$\n-2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2+1-1=-2.\n$$"}]}
